'The graphs resulting from model follow a similar shape to the model from the study done by David Pollard at Oregon state. Both the area and volume cross section followed the same trend and shape. Similar studies have used various modeling techniques for glacial cycles and produced similar results. A study by Chris Zweck in 2005 used an equation with more parameters and produced a similar result. The main difference between this study and the model we produced is that the large drop in area and volume is not present. Studies modeling sea level height along with ice sheets also show similar results to our model. A model of sea level by A.N.Ploskov shows a trend of sea level rise that matches with the ice sheet models from our model and the model made by Pollard. Despite the similar shape, our model does produce data values different from the previous studies. This could be due to errors in our calculations or  a difference in conditions accounted for in each study. Further studies could be done through more changing of parameters and potentially increasing the number of factors studied.
 
